Privacy Policy
Real Estate Dominance
Twelve52 LLC

Last updated: October 4, 2026

Real Estate Dominance ("the App") is developed by Twelve52 LLC ("we", "us", "our"). This policy explains what information is collected when you use the App, by whom, and why.

No account, no personal details. The App does not ask for your name, email address or any other personal details, and it works without an account.

Game data. Your saves, settings and progress are stored on your device. If you turn on cloud save, the same data is also stored in your own Google Play Games account so you can continue on another device. We do not have access to it.

Feedback and bug reports. If you choose to send feedback or report a bug from Settings, the text you type is sent to our server together with the App version, your platform and device model, the App language, and a fingerprint of your current save (a seed and week number, so we can reproduce a bug). Nothing identifies you personally unless you write it in the message. Reports are read by us and kept only as long as needed to act on them.

Remote settings. At launch the App reads balance settings, in-app announcements, language packs and the list of our other games from our server (hosted by Supabase). These are read-only downloads; the request carries no account or advertising identifier.

Advertising (Google AdMob). The App shows ads through Google AdMob. Google may collect device identifiers, IP address and usage data to serve and measure ads, personalized or not depending on your choices. In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland the App first shows Google's consent form. You can change your ad privacy choices at any time from the App's Settings and in your device settings. Google's privacy policy: policies.google.com/privacy.

Analytics (Firebase). The App uses Google Firebase Analytics for two things only: attribution of app installs to our advertising, and ad revenue reporting. It records app installs, purchases, ad impressions and one gameplay event (a game week resolved). No screens, no profiles, no personal details. Collection starts only after the consent steps above. Firebase's privacy information: firebase.google.com/support/privacy.

Google Play Games. If you sign in, Google handles your profile, achievements and leaderboard entries under its own privacy policy.

In-app purchases. Purchases are processed entirely by Google Play. We never see or store payment information.

A game, not advice. The App is a simulation. Nothing in it is financial, legal, tax or investment advice.

Children. The App is rated for a general audience and does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. The advertising described above applies to all players.

Retention. Reports are deleted once resolved or after 12 months at most. Everything else lives on your device or in your own cloud account and is removed when you delete the App or the account data.

Your choices. Reset or delete your advertising ID in your device settings (Settings > Privacy > Ads), open the ad privacy options in the App's Settings, buy Remove Ads to stop banner and interstitial ads, or turn cloud save off in Settings.

Changes. Updates to this policy appear on this page with a new date.

